\title{A \code{\verb~|let~} inside an evaluated term must be zeta by sharing, not a variable}
\taxon{Insight}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{machine}
\tag{nat}
\tag{soundness}
\meta{origin}{docs/design/RECONCILIATION.md}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Source: erratum E1 of \src{docs/design/RECONCILIATION.md}, section 5, which corrects \src{docs/design/ISA.md}; decision D9 of \src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M2.md}; [the session on the machine](ses-Z72N). Found by implementation on the Cedar slice.}
\ul{
\li{The instruction-set document made every \code{\verb~|let~} value a suspension with a flag, so that every value built from an evaluated \code{\verb~|let~} carried the mark "contains a free variable". That is the official behaviour only for the let variable of \code{\verb~|infer_let~}.}
\li{For a \code{\verb~|let~} inside a term that is evaluated, the body of an unfolded definition or a forced argument, the official \code{\verb~|whnf_core~} instantiates the body with the value: there is no variable.}
\li{With the rule of the document, lazy delta skipped the folding of Nat literals and conversion skipped the shortcut for \code{\verb~|Bool.true~} exactly where the official kernel folds, and the machine unfolded division, modulo and gcd on large literals by their fuel recursion: five Cedar declarations at about 1,000 times the official work.}
\li{The rule now: evaluation treats a \code{\verb~|let~} as zeta by sharing with a plain value, like the argument of a beta step; only the let variable of inference is a flagged suspension. The mark on a value means what the official \code{\verb~|has_fvar~} means. Code blocks emit a let value as an ordinary argument operand.}
}
\transclude{ex-GZ10}
\p{The document had said that over-approximating the mark is harmless because it only steers guards. It steers them into non-termination. The let variable of inference had its own correction later, see [the declared type of a let](ex-GZ3D).}
\p{See also: [the design review and its reconciliation](design-review-reconciliation); [evaluation and tabling](design-evaluation-and-tabling).}
